  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1...\n\nUpper ridge will begin to slowly break down starting today, with \nshowers and storms developing across the area, particularly this \nafternoon and evening. Very  unstable air, with CAPE values progged \nto be 3000-4000 J/kg, combined with drier air in lower levels of the \natmosphere/DCAPE greater than 1000 J/kg, will warrant the potential \nfor severe/downburst threat with any storms. SPC continues to \nhighlight the area in a slight risk for severe for today.\n\nIn addition, any storms during the period will contain heavy \ndownpours, and localized flooding issues are possible, particularly \nin spots that receive repetitive downpours. \n\nAdditional rounds of storms are expected Sunday into early next \nweek, with the approach of a shortwave trough. The threat for at \nleast isolated strong to severe storms also looks to be possible \nduring the period. \n\n\nKEY MESSAGE 2...\n\nStill some questions remain as to whether we will reach heat \ncriteria levels on Saturday, particularly with the threat for \nincreased convection, and cloud cover. However, due to the \nIndependence Day holiday, and the fact that hot and humid conditions \nwill persist, and with the area already several days into this \npattern, have elected to continue headlines into Saturday evening.\n\nSunday could touch heat advisory criteria in a few locations, but, \nwith scattered convection and cloud cover, thinking coverage will \nnot be enough to warrant continuation of headlines at this time.",
